        "problem": "Which of the following diagrams shows all the $6$th roots of unity?",
        "worked_solution": "Geometrically, the $6$th roots of unity have the following properties:\n\n- all of them lie on the unit circle centered in the origin,\n\n- one of the roots is $1,$ corresponding to the point $(1,0)$ on the complex plane,\n\n- the roots form a regular hexagon (regular $6$-sided polygon).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043589/assets/923d1a1b87833551ae6c451f15a6b5d8bdd75623e8d5c20e86357894bc24683d.png)",
